  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lifesaving WASH services for vulnerable SS Refugees, IDPs and host communities in White Nile state</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the April 2023 conflict between the Rapid Support Forces and Sudanese Armed Forces, Sudan has been in the midst of a severe humanitarian crisis, marked by widespread food insecurity and
limited access to basic services. Despite ongoing efforts to address the crisis, it remains severely underfunded. CAFOD&apos;s Multi-Sectoral Needs Assessment in White Nile States identified urgent needs and recommendations for targeted interventions, focusing on key vulnerabilities and cross-cutting issues like gender equality and
environmental sustainability, and confirming that a multi-sectoral response is required to address complex needs.</narrative>
  </description>
